{"type":"message","id":"4956ff7b","parentId":"b9d7bf59","timestamp":"2026-03-31T05:41:59.893Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Chrome is open with the page. The title shows the page is some kind of system (showing some Chinese characters that got garbled but it's likely the login page). Now I need to use UI automation to fill in the username and password fields.\n\nLet me write a script to find the input fields and fill them in. I'll use UIAutomation to find the Chrome window and its child elements.","thinkingSignature":"211e99e22b50249d82589542af4ef93151145a51b275361e327fb4be9ecb891a"},{"type":"text","text":"Chrome已打开，页面正在加载中。现在我用UI自动化填入账号密码：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_j2vfhu0h6e23_1","name":"write","arguments":{"content":"Add-Type -AssemblyName UIAutomationClient\nAdd-Type -AssemblyName UIAutomationTypes\n\nfunction Get-ChildElementsByControlType($element, $controlType) {\n    $condition = New-Object System.Windows.Automation.PropertyCondition([System.Windows.Automation.AutomationElement]::ControlTypeProperty, $controlType)\n    return $element.FindAll('Children', $condition)\n}\n\nfunction Find-InputField($element) {\n    $editCondition = New-Object System.Windows.Automation.PropertyCondition([System.Windows.Automation.AutomationElement]::ControlTypeProperty, [System.Windows.Automation.ControlType]::Edit)\n    return $element.FindFirst('Children', $editCondition)\n}\n\n$procs = Get-Process -Name chrome -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue | Where-Object { $_.MainWindowHandle -ne 0 }\nif (-not $procs) {\n    Write-Host \"No Chrome window found\"\n    exit 1\n}\n\n$chromeProc = $procs | Select-Object -First 1\nWrite-Host \"Using Chrome PID: $($chromeProc.Id)\"\n\n$chromeWindow = [System.Windows.Automation.AutomationElement]::FromHandle($chromeProc.MainWindowHandle)\nif (-not $chromeWindow) {\n    Write-Host \"Could not get automation element from window handle\"\n    exit 1\n}\n\nWrite-Host \"Window found, searching for input fields...\"\n\n# Find all Edit controls\n$editCondition = New-Object System.Windows.Automation.PropertyCondition([System.Windows.Automation.AutomationElement]::ControlTypeProperty, [System.Windows.Automation.ControlType]::Edit)\n$editFields = $chromeWindow.FindAll('Children', $editCondition)\n\n$count = 0\nforeach ($field in $editFields) {\n    $count++\n    $name = $field.Current.Name\n    $autoid = $field.Current.AutomationId\n    $rect = $field.Current.BoundingRectangle\n    Write-Host \"Field $count : Name='$name' AutoId='$autoid' Rect=$rect\"\n}\n\nif ($count -ge 2) {\n    # Fill first field (username)\n    $field1 = $editFields[0]\n    $field1.SetFocus()\n    Start-Sleep -Milliseconds 200\n    \n    $valPattern1 = $field1.GetCurrentPattern([System.Windows.Automation.ValuePattern]::Pattern) -as [System.Windows.Automation.ValuePattern]\n    if ($valPattern1) {\n        $valPattern1.SetValue(\"18926879306\")\n        Write-Host \"Filled username field\"\n    }\n    \n    # Fill second field (password)\n    $field2 = $editFields[1]\n    $field2.SetFocus()\n    Start-Sleep -Milliseconds 200\n    \n    $valPattern2 = $field2.GetCurrentPattern([System.Windows.Automation.ValuePattern]::Pattern) -as [System.Windows.Automation.ValuePattern]\n    if ($valPattern2) {\n        $valPattern2.SetValue(\"100911yzpYZP\")\n        Write-Host \"Filled password field\"\n    }\n    \n    Write-Host \"Done! Please click the login button manually.\"\n} else {\n    Write-Host \"Found only $count input fields, may need to wait for page to load\"\n}\n","file_path":"C:\\Users\\Administrator\\.openclaw\\workspace\\fill_login.ps1"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":2945,"output":806,"cacheRead":19925,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":23676,"cost":{"input":0.0008835,"output":0.0009672,"cacheRead":0.0011955,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0030461999999999998}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774935699780,"responseId":"061a9194e